{"title":"Career Roadmap: Radio Jockey","role":"Radio Jockey","summary":"A Radio Jockey (RJ) presents radio programmes, interacts with audiences, introduces music/content, conducts interviews, discusses current topics and creates engaging audio programming.","facts":{"Current degree":"Humanities & Social Sciences","Course":"BA (Bachelor of Arts – General / Honours)"},"about":[{"label":"Primary Goal","text":"Build professional voice, language, presentation, broadcasting, audio-production, content, audience-engagement and media skills for radio and digital audio careers"}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Roadmap Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Radio Jockey (RJ) presents radio programmes, interacts with audiences, introduces music/content, conducts interviews, discusses current topics and creates engaging audio programming."},{"type":"p","text":"Modern RJs may work beyond traditional FM radio in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"FM/AM radio"},{"text":"Internet radio"},{"text":"Podcasts"},{"text":"Digital audio platforms"},{"text":"YouTube/audio-video channels"},{"text":"News and entertainment media"},{"text":"Brand content"},{"text":"Live events"},{"text":"Voice-over"},{"text":"Audio advertising"},{"text":"Community broadcasting"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A regional-language BA provides a strong foundation in language, literature, pronunciation, cultural context and communication, but professional RJ work requires substantial practice in voice modulation, scripting, interviewing, audio production and live presentation."}]},{"heading":"What to Build During UG","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Build This","Learn From","Proof to Create","Gap to Avoid"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Language + communication"},{"text":"Pronunciation, literature, grammar, public speaking"},{"text":"Voice recordings + presentation portfolio"},{"text":"Weak pronunciation"}],[{"text":"